            <ArticleTitle>Clinical approaches to low back pain. Part 2. Management, sequelae, and disability and compensation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>490-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The management and psychologic sequelae of low back pain are discussed. We examine surgery as an option. Questions of disability and compensation, and the physician's role in these processes are examined.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
